# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Per-platform venvs — the Mac uses .venv-macos over the share.
.venv-*/

# Agent instructions stay OUT of every repo under energy-solution. They are
# workspace- and machine-specific context, not part of the product: they name
# local paths, the SMB share, and how this particular box is set up, none of
# which is true for anyone who clones this. The workspace copy lives one level
# up, outside any repo.
#
# CLAUDE.md is the ONE exception, added 2026-08-20. It carries the nehsa-net
# billing-lock CI rule, which is the opposite of machine-specific: it is about
# this repo's own GitHub Actions runs, it is identical in every nehsa-net repo,
# and it is needed exactly by someone who cloned this and is staring at a red
# check they did not cause. Nothing local-only goes in it — if that changes,
# this exception comes out with it.
.claude/
